---
name: clock
description: The user's time zone, local date and time, and the dates of the coming week. "Today" must be the user's date, not the server's UTC date; the dates are listed because small models get "tomorrow" wrong when they add it up themselves.
template:
  format:
    kind: mustache
  parser:
    kind: prompty
inputs:
  timeZone:
    kind: string
    description: "IANA time zone id"
    example: "Asia/Kolkata"
  today:
    kind: string
    description: "the user's local date, yyyy-MM-dd"
    example: "2026-10-01"
  now:
    kind: string
    description: "the user's local time, HH:mm"
    example: "09:30"
  tomorrow:
    kind: string
    description: "the user's local date tomorrow, yyyy-MM-dd"
    example: "2026-10-02"
  week:
    kind: array
    description: "the next seven days, one per line, \"Thursday 2026-10-01\""
    example:
      - "Thursday 2026-10-01 (today)"
      - "Friday 2026-10-02 (tomorrow)"
      - "Saturday 2026-10-03"
---
The user's time zone is {{timeZone}}, where today is {{today}} and the time is {{now}}. Tomorrow is {{tomorrow}}. Use these dates for "today", "tomorrow" and weekdays; never work a date out yourself:
{{#week}}
- {{.}}
{{/week}}
